# aether lint -- curated to signal, not style. clangd and run-clang-tidy read this file. The CI
# clang-tidy job runs it with warnings as errors, and with the analyzer starting paths in header
# functions too, over every translation unit outside test/ that its macOS build compiles. That
# covers each public header alone, the examples, src and bench, but not the Windows socket source or
# the opt-in comparison benchmark. A template is checked through the instantiations those units
# make, so one that only test/ instantiates is outside the gate. HeaderFilterRegex names the header
# directories rather than the checkout, whose path varies.
#
# The stock readability/modernize/misc checks fight the deliberate dense one-liners
# (braces-around-statements), the lowercase literal suffixes, the C arrays and explicit types, none
# of which are bugs. So only the bug, performance, portability and analyzer families below are on,
# minus the checks that flag intended code here:
#   branch-clone: `if constexpr` chains, and switch cases that map several values alike
#   incorrect-roundings: non-negative quantization
#   easily-swappable-parameters: same-typed parameter runs (crypto primitives, new* constructors)
#   enum-size: the int-based API enums; the wire enums already declare a one-byte base
#   avoid-pragma-once: every header uses #pragma once, not include guards
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -bugprone-incorrect-roundings,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '/(include/aether|examples|src)/'
